  "186": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "subject_definitions:\\n<Picture 1> is the supplied photograph photo_2.jpg, showing the restaurant hall with wooden tables, chairs, and decorated windows. Preserve its actual room, furniture, arrangement, and visual details.\\n<Picture 2> is the supplied photograph photo_7.jpg, showing thin raw pork, scallions, lettuce, and perilla leaves in dishes. Preserve the food, dishes, colors, and arrangement.\\n<Picture 3> is the supplied photograph photo_8.jpg, showing thin pork and garlic on a stone-style grill plate. Preserve the grill plate and the food's original shape and placement.\\n<Picture 4> is the supplied photograph photo_1.jpg, showing the restaurant's wall clock, self-service side-dish counter, utensils, and sauces. Preserve the actual interior and counter arrangement.\\n<Picture 5> is the supplied photograph photo_10.jpg, showing kimchi, greens, garlic, peppers, tofu, and side dishes on a table. Preserve the actual dishes and their arrangement.\\n<Subject 1> is the consistent off-screen narrator, identified as S1. Use <Audio 1> as the voice reference.\\nsummary:\\n[reference generation] Create a fifteen-second Korean short-form food video in which an unresolved dinner choice turns into a decision for samgyeopsal at Samsamjip. Follow the supplied photographs in order: restaurant hall, pork and greens, pork and garlic on the grill, the side-dish counter, and a complete table of side dishes. Use an off-screen narrator, not an on-camera speaker.\\nretention_analysis:\\nKeep the real restaurant hall, food, grill, dishes, and side-dish counter faithful to their supplied photographs. Do not invent or alter the restaurant's layout, food, or services. Use only subtle camera movement and restrained steam; keep the shape and arrangement of the food intact. The narrator is not visible. Use <Audio 1> only as a voice-character reference for S1; do not copy its original speech or audio signal. Do not create any on-screen text, captions, subtitles, or titles.\\ndetailed_description:\\nCreate a continuous fifteen-second video with five clear cuts, matching the supplied reference images and the timing below. Use natural, appetizing restaurant lighting and restrained camera motion. Keep the source photographs' actual backgrounds and subjects recognizable and unchanged.\\n[Shot 1] At 00:00.000, use <Picture 1>. Open on the restaurant hall with a gentle push toward the tables, establishing the dinner-choice setting. S1 speaks off-screen in Korean, clearly and conversationally, with a light questioning tone. Match <Audio 1> for voice character and do not assign a new voice quality. (S1) <d>[Korean] 저녁 메뉴, 아직도 고민?</d>\\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.500, cut to <Picture 2>. Make a restrained close-in move from the thin pork toward the scallions and greens; preserve the original food shapes and dishes. S1 continues off-screen with a decisive, friendly delivery. (S1) <d>[Korean] 삼겹살에 쌈채소면 답 나왔죠.</d>\\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.500, cut to <Picture 3>. Show the pork and garlic on the stone-style grill with a subtle hint of heat or steam. Keep the meat and garlic stable and faithful to the reference; do not add food. S1 speaks off-screen with a lively but natural rhythm. (S1) <d>[Korean] 돌판 위 마늘까지 함께 굽고,</d>\\n[Shot 4] At 00:08.500, cut to <Picture 4>. Briefly show the actual side-dish counter and its surrounding interior with a slow, minimal camera move. Preserve the wall clock, counter, utensils, and arrangement. S1 speaks off-screen. (S1) <d>[Korean] 반찬 코너에서 취향대로 더해,</d>\\n[Shot 5] At 00:11.500, cut to <Picture 5>. Reveal the full table, then make a gentle push toward the kimchi and greens while keeping all dishes and their arrangement intact. Finish on the complete table. S1 delivers the closing line warmly and clearly; finish the entire line before the video ends. (S1) <d>[Korean] 김치랑 쌈채소까지, 저녁 고민 끝!</d>\\nEach line is spoken once by the same off-screen narrator, S1. Keep the Korean speech natural, intelligible, and paced to fit each shot. Do not add dialogue, repeated lines, an on-camera speaker, or background vocals.\\noverall_soundscape:\\nUse subtle, natural restaurant room tone beneath the narration. Add a restrained grill sizzle during the grill shot and soft transitions between cuts. Keep effects secondary so the narrator and instrumental music remain clear.\\nnon_diegetic_music:\\nGenerate instrumental background music throughout the full fifteen seconds. Use a warm, upbeat Korean food-short rhythm with a light percussive pulse and a memorable melodic progression that builds gently toward the final table shot. Keep both the melody and rhythm distinctly audible while balancing them so every spoken Korean line remains crisp and intelligible. No vocals."
    },
